<|fim_suf|>, and recommender systems.

To give you an example of each, let's say we have a dataset of images of animals, along with their corresponding labels as either "dog" or "cat". Using supervised learning, we could train a deep neural network to classify new images as either a dog or a cat based on their features. In unsupervised learning, we could use clustering algorithms to group similar images together based on their visual features, without any prior knowledge of whether they are a dog or a cat. <|endoftext|>
