How did the haiku form originate?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Haiku originated in Japan in the 17th century. It was originally known as hokku, and was the first stanza of a collaborative linked-verse poem called a renku. Over time, poets began to write standalone hokku, which evolved into the modern-day haiku. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What are some common themes found in haiku poetry?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
