<|end|>
<|user|>
How does machine learning differ from traditional programming?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Traditional programming involves writing code that explicitly tells a computer what to do in every situation. Machine learning, <|fim_suf|>, involves training a computer to recognize patterns in data and make decisions based on that data. Instead of being explicitly programmed, a machine learning model is trained using large amounts of data and tweaks its own internal parameters to improve its performance. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Can you explain what deep learning is and how it relates to machine learning?
