<|fim_suf|>, which allows you to test if a condition is true or false and then perform a certain action depending on the result.

In this case, the formula starts by searching for the first brand name in cell A2 of your Excel sheet. If the SEARCH function finds the brand name, it returns a number. The ISNUMBER function then checks if that number is greater than 0 (meaning the brand name was found). If the number is greater than 0, the formula returns the brand name. If the number is not greater than 0, the formula moves on to the next brand name and repeats the process. If none of the brand names are found in the text, the formula returns an empty string (represented by two sets of quotation marks with nothing in between).

You can modify the formula to include additional brands by adding more nested IF statements with additional SEARCH functions. Just make sure to separate each nested IF statement with commas and close the final set of parenthesis at the end. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


