<|user|>
Can you create an Excel table that identifies the brand mentioned in a given piece of text? 
Here is an example table:
| Text | Brand |
|-----------------------------------------------------------|-------------|
| The all-new system from Samsung is the next big thing. | Samsung |
| Apple's latest iPhone has a new camera system. | Apple |
| The new line of laptops from Dell is very popular. | Dell |
And here is the Excel formula that can be used to extract the brand name:
=IF(ISNUMBER(SEARCH("Samsung",A2)),"Samsung",IF(ISNUMBER(SEARCH("Apple",A2)),"Apple",IF(ISNUMBER(SEARCH("Dell",A2)),"Dell",""))) 
You can modify this formula to include additional brands as needed.
<|end|>
