Natural language processing (NLP) is a field of study that deals with the interaction between computers and human languages. NLP involves techniques such as text preprocessing, tokenization, part-of-speech tagging, named entity recognition, sentiment analysis, and more. These techniques help computers understand, interpret, and generate human language. <|endoftext|>
