How can I add conditional formatting to highlight the cells with sales above a certain threshold in Excel?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To add conditional formatting in Excel, follow these steps:
1. Select the range of cells that you want to apply the formatting to.
2. Click on the "Conditional Formatting" option in the "Home" tab.
3. Choose the "Highlight Cells Rules" option, and then select "Greater Than".
4. Enter the threshold value in the box, <|fim_suf|>, if you want to highlight all the cells with sales above $150, you would enter 150 in the box and choose a formatting style such as bold or color fill. This will automatically highlight all the cells in the selected range that meet this condition. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


<|fim_mid|>and choose the formatting style you want to apply.

