<|user|>
How does transfer learning relate to deep learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Transfer learning is a technique in machine learning where a model trained on one task is applied to a different but related task. In the context of deep learning, transfer learning involves taking a pre-trained deep neural network and using it as a starting point for a new task. This can be useful when there is not enough data to train a new model from scratch or when the new task is similar to the original task on which the model was trained. By leveraging the learned features from the pre-trained model, transfer learning can lead to faster convergence and better performance on the new task. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


