How does a computer mouse work?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
A computer mouse works by detecting motion relative to a surface. Inside the mouse, there is a ball or an optical sensor that tracks the movement of the mouse on the surface. This information is then sent to the computer, which uses it to move the cursor on the screen. The buttons on the mouse are used to perform various functions, such as selecting items and opening menus. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
