<|asst|>
Sure, I can help you with that! Here's an Excel formula that you can use to select a random punchline from your table and incorporate it into the sentence:
= "My boss is so mean that " & INDEX(A:A,RANDBETWEEN(1,COUNTA(A:A))) 
In this formula, "A:A" should be replaced with the column that contains your punchlines. This formula uses the RANDBETWEEN function to select a random row number from the range of cells containing your punchlines, and the INDEX function to retrieve the selected punchline. The "&" symbol is used to concatenate the selected punchline with the rest of the sentence. 
Once you enter this formula into a cell, it will generate a random witty punchline each time the worksheet is recalculated. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
