<|asst|>
Sure, the world's deepest ocean is the Pacific Ocean. It has an average depth of 12,080 feet (3,682 meters) and the deepest part of the ocean, known as the Challenger Deep, is located in the Mariana Trench, which is approximately 36,070 feet (10,994 meters) deep. <|endoftext|>
