| Product 4 | $40 | Description | Image |
[Excel Table Code]
=FILTER(A2:D5,(C2:C5>=20)*(C2:C5<=30)) 
This code will filter the products based on their price, displaying only those with prices between $20 and $30. We can also use Excel tables to create interactive product pages with tabs for different information, such as reviews and specifications. How can we further utilize Excel tables to enhance the user experience of an e-commerce website?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Excel tables can be used to display product information in a more organized and interactive way by using features such as conditional formatting, data validation, and drop-down lists. 
For example, you can use conditional formatting to highlight products that are on sale or have limited stock. You can use data validation to ensure that users enter valid information when searching for products or filling out forms. You can also create drop-down lists to make it easier for users to filter products by category, brand, or other criteria.
In addition, you can use Excel tables to create dynamic charts and graphs that display product sales trends, customer ratings, and other data. This can help users make more informed purchasing decisions and provide valuable insights for the e-commerce website's management team.
Overall, Excel tables can be a powerful tool for enhancing the user experience of an e-commerce website by providing organized, interactive, and visually appealing product information. <|endoftext|>
