<|user|>
What is the difference between machine learning and deep learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Machine learning and deep learning are both branches of the broader field of artificial intelligence, but they differ in their approach to learning from data. Machine learning algorithms are designed to learn from data by identifying patterns and making predictions based on those patterns. They do this by using statistical techniques to generalize from a set of examples.

Deep learning, on the other hand, is a subset of machine learning that uses artificial neural networks to learn from large amounts of data. These neural networks are modeled after the structure of the human brain and are designed to automatically extract features from raw data. This allows deep learning models to learn more complex representations of the input data, which can lead to better performance on tasks like image recognition and natural language processing.

In summary, while both machine learning and deep learning involve learning from data, deep learning takes a more complex approach by using artificial neural networks to extract higher-level representations of the data. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


