<|user|>
How can I calculate the surface area of a circle and square using JavaScript? Can you also provide a function to calculate the ratio of surface areas of a circle with radius [formula]r[/formula] to a square with side [formula]s[/formula]?
Here is a JavaScript function to calculate the surface area of a circle:
function circleSurfaceArea(r) {
 return Math.PI * r * r;
}
And here is a function to calculate the surface area of a square:
function squareSurfaceArea(s) {
 return s * s;
}
To find the ratio of the surface area of a circle with radius 4 cm to a square with side 4 cm, you can use these functions as follows:
var circleArea = circleSurfaceArea(4);
var squareArea = squareSurfaceArea(4);
var ratio = circleArea / squareArea;
The resulting ratio is [formula]${ratio}$[/formula].
<|end|>
