Yes, you can modify the table to store multiple opposite words for a single word by changing the structure of the table slightly. You can create a separate row for each opposite word associated with a word. Here is the modified SQL code for creating the table:
```
CREATE TABLE opposite_words (
 word VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
 opposite_word VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL
);
```
To insert data into the table, you can use the following SQL code:
```
INSERT INTO opposite_words (word, opposite_word)
VALUES
 ('bright', 'dim'),
 ('daylight', 'nighttime'),
 ('light', 'dark'),
 ('light', 'heavy');
```
To retrieve all the opposite words for "light", you can use the following SQL code:
```
SELECT opposite_word
FROM opposite_words
WHERE word = 'light';
```
This will give you the opposite words "dark" and "heavy". <|endoftext|>
