What is the difference between BBQ ribs and regular pork ribs?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
BBQ ribs are typically slow-cooked on a grill or smoker, while regular pork ribs may be cooked using a variety of methods including boiling, roasting, or grilling. BBQ ribs are also often seasoned with a dry rub or coated in a sauce before cooking, while regular pork ribs may simply be seasoned with salt and pepper. Additionally, BBQ ribs are typically meatier and more flavorful than regular pork ribs. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
