<|user|>
How can I determine the relationship between carbon emissions and global temperature increase over the past century? Additionally, can you provide a C++ code to calculate the yearly average of carbon emissions from a given dataset?
Here is a sample C++ code that can read a CSV file containing carbon emission data and compute the yearly average emission:
```c++
#include 
#include 
#include 
#include 
#include 
using namespace std;
int main()
{
 string line;
 ifstream myfile ("carbon_emissions.csv");
 vector emissions;
 double total_emission = 0;
 if (myfile.is_open())
 {
 while ( getline (myfile,line) )
 {
 stringstream ss(line);
 string token;
 // extract year and emission value
 getline(ss, token, ','); // year
 getline(ss, token, ','); // emission
 double emission = stod(token);
 emissions.push_back(emission);
 }
 myfile.close();
 // calculate average emission per year
 int num_years = emissions.size();
 double avg_emission = 0;
 for(int i=0; i<num_years; i++) {
 total_emission += emissions[i];
 }
 avg_emission = total_emission / num_years;
 cout << "Average carbon emission per year: " << avg_emission << endl;
 }
 return 0;
}
```
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To determine the relationship between carbon emissions and global temperature increase over the past century, you can use statistical analysis and modeling techniques. One commonly used approach is to perform a regression analysis, where you can model the relationship between carbon emissions and temperature increase over time. You can use historical data on carbon emissions and global temperature increase to estimate the parameters of the model and assess the strength of the relationship.
Regarding the C++ code, the sample code you provided reads a CSV file containing carbon emission data and computes the yearly average emission. However, you will need to provide the CSV file with the data to run the code successfully. Additionally, you may need to modify the code to suit your specific data format and requirements. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
