If you prefer using Python, you can use the "matplotlib" library which provides a wide range of functions for creating different types of plots, including line charts, scatterplots, and heatmaps. You can also use the "seaborn" library, which provides high-level interfaces for creating sophisticated statistical visualizations.
Overall, there are many open-source tools and libraries that can help you visualize the relationship between carbon emissions and global temperature increase. The choice of tool or library may depend on your specific requirements and preferences. <|endoftext|>
