<|user|>
What is the origin of the Haiku poem and how has it evolved over time?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The Haiku originated in Japan during the Edo period (1603-1868) and was known as Hokku. It was originally used as an opening stanza for a series of linked poems called renga. Over time, Hokku became its own standalone form of poetry and eventually evolved into the Haiku we know today. In the 20th century, Haiku spread throughout the world and became popular in many different languages and cultures, leading to new variations and interpretations of the form. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
