Yes, there are several idioms in French that convey a similar idea to "une aiguille dans une botte de foin". One such phrase is "chercher une épingle dans une meule de foin", which translates to "searching for a pin in a haystack". This expression is similar to the English idiom, but uses the word "pin" instead of "needle".

Another French expression that conveys a similar meaning is "un grain de sable dans les rouages", which translates to "a grain of sand in the gears". This phrase is used to describe a small problem or obstacle that can cause significant difficulties, much like how finding a needle in a haystack can be a challenging task. <|endoftext|>
