Can you explain the concept of quantum entanglement?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Quantum entanglement is a phenomenon that occurs when two particles become connected in such a way that the state of one particle can be determined by the state of the other particle, even if they are separated by large distances. This means that if you measure the properties of one particle, such as its spin or polarization, the other particle will immediately have a correlated property, regardless of how far apart they are. This is because the two particles are described by a single quantum state, which encompasses both particles. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
