How can I search for at least 3 specific characters within a text file using C++? The text file is a part of a larger program analyzing the book Animal Farm.
Here is an Excel table showing the characters I want to search for:
| Character | ASCII Code |
|-----------|------------|
| a | 97 |
| b | 98 |
| c | 99 |
And here is the C++ code I have so far for reading the text file:
#include 
#include 
#include 
using namespace std;
int main() {
 string line;
 ifstream myfile ("AnimalFarm.txt");
 if (myfile.is_open())
 {
 while (getline (myfile,line))
 {
 cout << line << 'n';
 }
 myfile.close();
 }
 else cout << "Unable to open file";
 return 0;
}
How can I modify this code to search for the characters in the table and return their positions within the text file?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can modify the code to search for the characters in the text file by looping through each character in each line of the file and comparing it to the ASCII codes of the characters you want to search for. Here is an example code snippet that should work:
```
#include 
#include 
#include 
using namespace std;
int main() {
 string line;
 ifstream myfile("AnimalFarm.txt");
 if (myfile.is_open()) {
 int line_num = 1;
 while (getline(myfile, line)) {
 for (int i = 0; i < line.length(); i++) {
 if (line[i] == 'a' || line[i] == 'b' || line[i] == 'c') {
 cout << "Found character " << line[i] << " at line " << line_num << ", position " << i+1 << endl;
 }
 }
 line_num++;
 }
 myfile.close();
 }
 else {
 cout << "Unable to open file" << endl;
 }
 return 0;
}
```
This code loops through each line of the file and then loops through each character in the line. If the character matches one of the characters you want to search for, it prints out the character, the line number, and the position within the line. You can modify the if statement to add more characters to search for. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How can I modify this code to also search for whole words that contain the characters I want to search for? For example, if I want to search for the word "cat" and it appears in the text file as "scatter", how can I find it?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To modify the code to search for whole words that contain the characters you want to search for, you can use the `find` function of the `string` class. Here is an updated code snippet that should work for your needs:

```
#include 
#include 
#include 
using namespace std;
int main() {
 string line;
 ifstream myfile("AnimalFarm.txt");
 if (myfile.is_open()) {
 int line_num = 1;
 while (getline(myfile, line)) {
 size_t pos;
 for (int i = 0; i < line.length(); i++) {
 if (line[i] == 'a' || line[i] == 'b' || line[i] == 'c') {
 pos = line.find("cat", i);
 if (pos != string::npos) {
 cout << "Found word containing "cat" at line " << line_num << ", position " << pos+1 << endl;
 i = pos + 2;
 }
 }
 }
 line_num++;
 }
 myfile.close();
 }
 else {
 cout << "Unable to open file" << endl;
 }
 return 0;
}
```

This code uses the `find` function to search for the word "cat" starting from the current character position in the line. If it finds a match, it prints out the line number and the position of the match within the line. The `i` variable is then set to the position after the end of the match so that we don't find the same match again. You can modify the word to search for by changing the string argument of the `find` function. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


