<|user|>
Find and provide two sources to support the following statement
The economic cost of climate change is estimated in trillions of dollars.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
1. According to a report published by the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC), the economic cost of climate change could range from 2% to 10% of global GDP by the end of the century. This amounts to trillions of dollars in losses. (Source: IPCC, 2014)

2. A study conducted by the Stanford Institute for Economic Policy Research found that unmitigated climate damage could cost the world economy as much as $24 trillion by the end of the century. This study takes into account the economic impacts of rising sea levels, increased natural disasters, and decreased agricultural productivity, among other factors. (Source: <|fim_suf|>, 2018) <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
