Furthermore, research conducted at the University of East London found that drinking water during an exam can improve performance on cognitive tasks, especially those related to short-term memory. The exact mechanisms by which hydration impacts the brain are still being studied, but it is clear that staying properly hydrated is essential for optimal cognitive function. <|endoftext|>
