<|user|>
Can you explain the concept of cognitive dissonance?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Cognitive dissonance is a psychological concept that refers to the mental discomfort experienced by an individual who holds two or more contradictory beliefs, values, or attitudes at the same time. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How can cognitive dissonance be reduced or resolved?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
There are several ways to reduce or resolve cognitive dissonance. One way is to change one's behavior to align with their beliefs or values. Another way is to change one's beliefs or values to align with their behavior. A third way is to seek out information that supports their beliefs or values. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
