# Finding the table containing the dwarf planet information
table = soup.find('table', {'class': 'wikitable sortable'})
# Finding all the rows in the table
rows = table.find_all('tr')
# Creating an empty list to store the dwarf planet names
dwarf_planets = []
# Looping through each row in the table and extracting the dwarf planet name
for row in rows[1:]:
 cells = row.find_all('td')
 name = cells[0].text.strip()
 dwarf_planets.append(name)
# Printing the list of dwarf planet names
print(dwarf_planets)
```
This code uses the `requests` library to send a GET request to the Wikipedia page containing the list of possible dwarf planets. It then uses BeautifulSoup to parse the HTML content of the page and find the table containing the dwarf planet information. It loops through each row in the table and extracts the name of the dwarf planet, which is then added to a list. Finally, the code prints the list of dwarf planet names. <|endoftext|>
