Yes, there are currently five recognized dwarf planets in our solar system in addition to Pluto: Ceres, Eris, Haumea, Makemake, and Haumea. Ceres is located in the asteroid belt between Mars and Jupiter, while Eris, Haumea, and Makemake are all located in the Kuiper Belt. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


