<|user|>
What is a RESTful API?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
A RESTful API is an architectural style for building web services that uses HTTP requests to access and manipulate data. It is based on a set of principles, including using standard HTTP methods (such as GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) to perform operations on resources, and using URLs to identify and locate resources. A well-designed RESTful API should be stateless, meaning it does not require the server to retain any information between requests. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What is the difference between machine learning and deep learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Machine learning is a subset of artificial intelligence (AI) that involves teaching machines to learn from data, without being explicitly programmed. Deep learning is a specific type of machine learning that uses neural networks to model and solve complex problems. The main difference between machine learning and deep learning is that deep learning algorithms can learn from more complex data than traditional machine learning algorithms, due to the ability of neural networks to model non-linear relationships between features. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


