<|user|>
What is the difference between an adjective and an adverb?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
An adjective describes a noun or pronoun, while an adverb describes a verb, adjective, or other adverb. For example, in the sentence "She is a fast runner," "fast" is an adjective describing the noun "runner." In the sentence "She ran quickly," "quickly" is an adverb describing the verb "ran." <|endoftext|>
