{"summary": "The Eiffel Tower is a wrought-iron lattice tower on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France. It is named after the engineer Gustave Eiffel, whose company designed and built the tower. Constructed from 1887 to 1889 as the entrance to the 1889 World's Fair, it was initially criticized by some of France's leading artists and intellectuals for its design, but it has become a global cultural icon of France and one of the most recognisable structures in the world."}
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The Eiffel Tower is a wrought-iron lattice tower located on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France. It was designed and built by the company of engineer Gustave Eiffel between 1887 and 1889 as the entrance to the 1889 World's Fair. Despite initial criticism from France's leading artists and intellectuals, it has since become a global cultural icon of France and one of the most recognisable structures in the world. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
That's interesting. Can you tell me more about Gustave Eiffel?
