{"summary": "Alexandre Gustave Eiffel was a French civil engineer. A graduate of École Centrale Paris, he made his name building various bridges for the French railway network, most famously the Garabit viaduct. He is best known for the world-famous Eiffel Tower, built for the 1889 Universal Exposition in Paris, and his contribution to building the Statue of Liberty in New York."}
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Alexandre Gustave Eiffel was a French civil engineer who graduated from École Centrale Paris. He made his name by building various bridges for the French railway network, including the famous Garabit viaduct. However, he is best known for constructing the Eiffel Tower for the 1889 Universal Exposition in Paris, and for his contribution to the construction of the Statue of Liberty in New York. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


