Using the [HTML page] data format, create a webpage that displays a list of 7 words related to the word "party". Each word should be displayed in a separate list item and should be accompanied by an image related to the word. How would you go about creating this webpage using HTML and CSS?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To create a webpage that displays a list of 7 words related to the word "party" with accompanying images, you can follow these steps:
1. Create an HTML file with the basic structure of a webpage, including the head and body tags.
2. Within the body tag, create an unordered list using the ul and li tags. This will be the container for your list of words and images.
3. For each list item, create another unordered list using the ul and li tags. This will be the container for the word and image.
4. Within each nested unordered list, add an image tag using the img tag. Set the source attribute to the URL of the image you want to use. You can also add an alt attribute to provide alternative text for the image.
5. After the image tag, add a text description of the word using the p tag.
6. Repeat steps 3-5 for each list item.
7. Use CSS to style the list items, images, and text as desired. You can use properties like font-size, color, padding, and margin to adjust the appearance of the elements.
Here is an example HTML code that you can use as a starting point:
```html

Party Words

 /* CSS styles go here */
 
Party Words
===========
* + ![Balloons](https://example.com/balloons.jpg)
	+ Balloons
* + ![Cake](https://example.com/cake.jpg)
	+ Cake
* + ![Confetti](https://example.com/confetti.jpg)
	+ Confetti
* + ![Dancing](https://example.com/dancing.jpg)
	+ Dancing
* + ![Drinks](https://example.com/drinks.jpg)
	+ Drinks
* + ![Music](https://example.com/music.jpg)
	+ Music
* + ![Party Hat](https:<|fim_mid|>//example.com/party-hat.jpg)
	+ Party Hat


```
