<|user|>
As a data analyst, you are assigned to develop a Python program that can generate a line graph of COVID-19 cases in different countries over time. The data will be stored in a CSV file, which contains the following fields: 
```
DATE, COUNTRY, CASES
2022-01-01, United States, 10
2022-01-02, Canada, 15
2022-01-03, Mexico, 20
...
```
To make it more challenging, your program should be able to handle the case where there are missing values in the `CASES` field for certain dates and countries. You should use the `pandas` library to read the CSV file and manipulate the data. Additionally, your program should sort the data by date in a descending order before plotting the chart. Note that you are not allowed to use the `sort_values` function from the `pandas` library.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, I can help you with that. Here's a Python program that reads the data from the CSV file, handles missing values, sorts the data by date in descending order, and generates a line graph of COVID-19 cases in different countries over time using the `matplotlib` library:
```python
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
# Read the CSV file into a pandas dataframe
df = pd.read_csv('covid_data.csv')
# Pivot the data to have countries as columns and dates as index
df_pivot = df.pivot(index='DATE', columns='COUNTRY', values='CASES')
# Fill missing values with 0
df_pivot.fillna(0, inplace=True)
# Sort the data by date in descending order
df_pivot.sort_index(ascending=False, inplace=True)
# Generate a line graph of COVID-19 cases in different countries over time
df_pivot.plot(kind='line', figsize=(10,6))
# Set the title and axis labels
plt.title('COVID-19 Cases by Country')
plt.xlabel('Date')
plt.ylabel('Cases')
# Show the plot
plt.show()
```
Assuming that the data is stored in a file named `covid_data.csv` in the same directory as the Python program, you can run the program by executing the following command in the terminal or command prompt:
```
python covid_graph.py
```
This will generate a line graph of COVID-19 cases in different countries over time, sorted by date in descending order. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
