Can you explain the difference between probability and statistics?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Probability is the branch of mathematics that deals with the likelihood of events occurring, while statistics is the study of data collection, analysis, interpretation, presentation, and organization. In other words, probability predicts what could happen in the future, while statistics looks at what has already happened in the past. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How is calculus used in physics?
<|end|>
