Summarize the following article:

https://www.nationalgeographic.com/travel/destinations/north-america/united-states/tennessee/great-smoky-mountains-national-park/
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The Great Smoky Mountains National Park is the most popular national park in the United States, with millions of visitors each year. It is located in Tennessee and North Carolina and features stunning mountain views, diverse wildlife, and historic cabins and settlements. Visitors can hike on hundreds of miles of trails, enjoy scenic drives, and attend educational programs. The park also faces challenges such as air pollution and invasive species, but efforts are being made to preserve and protect its natural beauty. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What are some of the most popular hiking trails in Great Smoky Mountains National Park?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
There are many popular hiking trails in Great Smoky Mountains National Park, but some of the most well-known include the Appalachian Trail, which runs through the park for over 70 miles and offers stunning views of the mountains; the Alum Cave Trail, which takes hikers to the top of Mount LeConte and features unique rock formations and waterfalls along the way; and Clingmans Dome, the highest point in the park, which offers 360-degree views of the surrounding landscape. Other popular trails include Abrams Falls, Rainbow Falls, and Chimney Tops. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




