Deductive reasoning is when you start with a general premise and apply it to specific cases, while inductive reasoning is when you start with specific cases and use them to form a general rule or principle. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Can you give me an example of deductive reasoning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! If we know that all humans are mortal and that John is a human, then we can deduce that John is mortal. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
And what about an example of inductive reasoning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
One example of inductive reasoning could be observing that every time a certain button is pressed on a remote control, <|fim_mid|>the TV turns off. Therefore<|fim_eom|>

