81 = 74 - 70cos(C)

Rearranging terms, we get:

cos(C) = (74 - 81) / (-140)

cos(C) = 0.04285714

Taking the arccosine of both sides, we get:

C = cos^-1(0.04285714)

C ≈ 86.46 degrees

So the angle between the sides of length 5 and 7 is approximately 86.46 degrees. <|endoftext|>
