<|end|>
<|asst|>
Climate change is expected to have significant impacts on global food production. Rising temperatures, changing precipitation patterns, and increased frequency of extreme weather events are likely to reduce crop yields and negatively affect food security in many parts of the world. In addition, changing temperatures and rainfall patterns may shift the geographic range of certain crops, affecting where they can be grown and potentially leading to conflicts over land use. Climate change is a complex and urgent issue that requires global action to mitigate its impact. <|endoftext|>
