What is the significance of Mount Everest to climbers and what are the risks involved in climbing it?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Mount Everest is the highest peak on Earth, and for many climbers, summiting it is considered the ultimate achievement. However, climbing Everest also carries significant risks, including altitude sickness, frostbite, high winds, and avalanches. In addition, the extreme physical demands of the climb can be overwhelming, and inexperienced climbers may find themselves unable to cope with the harsh conditions. Despite these risks, thousands of climbers attempt to summit Everest each year, drawn by the challenge and adventure that await them on the mountain. <|endoftext|>
