Aerobic exercise, such as running or cycling, requires oxygen to produce energy and can improve cardiovascular health, while anaerobic exercise, like weight lifting or sprinting, does not rely on oxygen and can increase muscular strength and power. Both types of exercise have unique benefits for the body and can be incorporated into a well-rounded fitness routine. <|endoftext|>
