Sure! Here are the steps to calculate the average and standard deviation of a set of data points in Excel:
1. Select the range of cells that contains the data points you want to analyze, including any column or row labels. In this case, select cells A1 through A10.
2. Click on the "Formulas" tab in the ribbon at the top of the Excel window.
3. In the "Function Library" group, click on the "More Functions" dropdown menu, then choose "Statistical" and select "AVERAGE" from the list.
4. In the "Function Arguments" dialog box that appears, select the range of cells that contains the data points you want to analyze. In this case, select cells A1 through A10.
5. Click "OK" to close the dialog box and calculate the average of the data points.
6. To calculate the standard deviation, repeat steps 2-4, but this time select "STDEV.S" from the list of statistical functions.
7. In the "Function Arguments" dialog box that appears, select the range of cells that contains the data points you want to analyze. In this case, select cells A1 through A10.
8. Click "OK" to close the dialog box and calculate the standard deviation of the data points.
