Weather refers to the short-term atmospheric conditions in a specific area, such as temperature, precipitation, humidity, and wind. Climate, on the other hand, refers to the average weather patterns and conditions over an extended period of time, typically spanning decades or longer. Climate takes into account factors like geographic location, prevailing winds, ocean currents, <|fim_suf|>, among others, and is used to describe long-term trends and patterns in weather. <|endoftext|>
