I found a recipe for Vegan Lasagna. The ingredients you will need are lasagna noodles, tomato sauce, vegan cheese, spinach, zucchini, and eggplant. Here are the instructions: Preheat oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). In a large pot of salted boiling water, <|fim_suf|>, and drain. In a large saucepan, cook and stir tomatoes, tomato sauce, green bell pepper, mushrooms, onion, water, garlic, basil, 2 teaspoons salt, and pepper until heated through. Layer a third of the lasagna noodles in the bottom of a 9x13 inch baking dish. Cover noodles with a half of the tofu mixture. Repeat. Cover lasagna with foil: to prevent sticking, either spray foil with cooking spray, or make sure the foil does not touch the lasagna. Bake for 25 minutes. Remove foil, and bake an additional 25 minutes. Allow to sit 15 minutes before serving. <|endoftext|>
