Can you explain the difference between global warming and climate change?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Global warming refers specifically to the long-term increase in Earth's average surface temperature, primarily caused by the burning of fossil fuels which releases greenhouse gases that trap heat in the atmosphere. Climate change encompasses a broader range of phenomena, including changes in precipitation patterns, sea level rise, and more frequent extreme weather events like hurricanes and droughts, all of which are driven by global warming as well as other factors. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
