<|user|>
What are some common data types in Python?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Python has several built-in data types, including integers, floating-point numbers, strings, booleans, and lists. Integers are whole numbers, while floating-point numbers are decimal numbers. Strings are sequences of characters, such as words and sentences. Booleans are either True or False values. Lists are ordered collections of values, which can be of any type. Additionally, there are other data types like tuples, sets, and dictionaries, each with their own unique properties and use cases. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


