<|end|>
<|user|>
Are there any other classic games that can be adapted for video chat?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Absolutely! "Pictionary" is another classic game that can work well over video chat. In this game, one person draws a picture of a word or phrase while the others try to guess what it is. You can use a virtual whiteboard or drawing app to make the drawing visible to all players. Another option is "Scattergories," where each player has a list of categories and has to come up with items that fit into those categories starting with a specific letter. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What about more cooperative games rather than competitive ones?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
For cooperative games, you might try "Keep Talking and Nobody Explodes." In this game, one player is given a bomb with various buttons, switches, and wires, while the other players have access to a manual with instructions for defusing the bomb. The catch is that the defusers can't see the bomb, so the players have to communicate effectively to prevent it from exploding. Another option is "Werewolf," where players work together to identify and eliminate the werewolves among them before they take over the group. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
