In this code, we first define a customized lexicon with domain-specific words and phrases that are important to the sentiment analysis of the given phrase. We then create a `SentimentIntensityAnalyzer` object from the NLTK library and add the customized lexicon to it using the `update()` method.
Finally, we test the sentiment analysis with the given phrase "He did an amazing job" and print the sentiment scores using the `polarity_scores()` method of the `SentimentIntensityAnalyzer` object.
The sentiment scores will be a dictionary with four keys: `neg`, `neu`, `pos`, and `compound`. The `compound` score represents an overall sentiment rating between -1 (most negative) and 1 (most positive), taking into account the customized lexicon. <|endoftext|>
