Can you explain the difference between supervised and unsupervised learning in machine learning? Give an example of each.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, supervised learning is a type of machine learning where the model is trained on labeled data. The goal is to map inputs to outputs based on the given data. Classification and regression are two common types of supervised learning. An example of supervised learning is image classification, where a model is trained to label images with certain objects or categories.

On the other hand, unsupervised learning is a type of machine learning where the model is trained on unlabeled data. The goal is to find patterns, structure, or relationships in the data. Clustering and dimensionality reduction are two common types of unsupervised learning. An example of unsupervised learning is customer segmentation, where a model is trained to group customers into different segments based on their purchasing behaviors without any prior knowledge about what those segments should be. <|endoftext|>
