<|user|>
Why do some people have allergies and others don't?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Allergies are caused by an overactive immune system. Some people may have a genetic predisposition to developing allergies, while others may develop them due to environmental factors such as exposure to certain allergens. The specific cause of allergies in each individual is not entirely clear, but it is believed to involve a combination of genetic and environmental factors. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
