<|user|>
Can you explain the difference between artificial intelligence and machine learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Artificial intelligence refers to computer systems that can perform tasks that typically require human-like intelligence, such as understanding natural language or recognizing images. Machine learning, <|fim_suf|>, is a subset of AI that involves training algorithms to make predictions or decisions based on data, without being explicitly programmed. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How does virtual reality work?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Virtual reality works by creating a simulated environment that can be experienced through a headset or other device. This is accomplished using a combination of hardware and software, including high-resolution displays, motion sensors, and powerful graphics processing units (GPUs) that can render complex 3D environments in real-time. When a user dons a VR headset, they are immersed in this simulated environment and can interact with it using specialized controllers or other peripherals. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


