One major inaccuracy is the size of the Velociraptors. In real life, they were much smaller than the ones depicted in the movie. Another issue is the way that the T-Rex is portrayed as being able to see only if something moves, whereas in reality, it had excellent vision. Additionally, the scene where the Dilophosaurus spits venom is entirely fictional, as there is no evidence that this species had such an ability. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Are there any dinosaurs in Jurassic Park that are accurately portrayed?
