<|user|>
How can I use a SQL database to generate a list of words related to managing stress and achieving work-life balance from the letters "S T E C O P L R A T E I Y F N"?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can use SQL's LIKE operator and pattern matching to generate a list of words related to managing stress and achieving work-life balance from the given letters. Here's an example SQL query that you can use:
```
SELECT word
FROM words
WHERE word LIKE '%s%'
 AND word LIKE '%t%'
 AND word LIKE '%e%'
 AND word LIKE '%c%'
 AND word LIKE '%o%'
 AND word LIKE '%p%'
 AND word LIKE '%l%'
 AND word LIKE '%r%'
 AND word LIKE '%a%'
 AND word LIKE '%t%'
 AND word LIKE '%i%'
 AND word LIKE '%y%'
 AND word LIKE '%f%'
 AND word LIKE '%n%'
```
In this example, `words` is the name of the table that contains the list of words you want to search through. The `%` symbol is used as a wildcard character to match any number of characters before or after the specified letter. The query will return all words that contain the letters "S T E C O P L R A T E I Y F N" in any order. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
