3. SQL Zoo: SQL Zoo provides interactive SQL tutorials that let you practice writing SQL queries against real-world databases.

4. Stanford Database Course on Coursera: The Stanford Database course on Coursera is a comprehensive course that covers relational databases and SQL in depth.

5. Head First SQL by Lynn Beighley: This book is a great resource for beginners who want to learn SQL in a fun and engaging way.

6. Learning SQL by Alan Beaulieu: <|fim_suf|>, including data manipulation, data definition, and database design.

Choose the resource that best fits your learning style and level of expertise. Good luck! <|endoftext|>
