What is the difference between syntax and semantics in programming languages?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Syntax refers to the formal rules that dictate how programs are written, including grammar, spelling, and punctuation. Semantics, on the other hand, is concerned with the meaning of those programs and how they operate. Essentially, syntax is about how code is structured and written, while semantics is about what the code does. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
