<|user|>
What would be the most efficient way to retrieve the nationality of Adolf Hitler from the SQL database "world_leaders"? The database has a table named "world_leaders" with columns such as "name", "nationality", and "birth_year". Please provide a Go code that considers multiple-step reasoning and complex logic to extract the desired information. [Latex code]usepackage{sql}begin{document}begin{lstlisting}[language=SQL] SELECT nationality FROM world_leaders WHERE name = 'Adolf Hitler' end{lstlisting}end{document
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a Go code snippet that retrieves the nationality of Adolf Hitler from the SQL database "world_leaders":
```
package main
import (
 "database/sql"
 "fmt"
 _ "github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql"
)
func main() {
 db, err := sql.Open("mysql", "user:password@tcp(127.0.0.1:3306)/world_leaders")
 if err != nil {
 panic(err.Error())
 }
 defer db.Close()
 var nationality string
 err = db.QueryRow("SELECT nationality FROM world_leaders WHERE name = 'Adolf Hitler'").Scan(&nationality)
 if err != nil {
 panic(err.Error())
 }
 fmt.Println("The nationality of Adolf Hitler is", nationality)
}
```
