3. In the United States, the cost of higher education has risen significantly faster than the rate of inflation over the past few decades. According to data from the National Center for Education Statistics, the average annual cost of tuition, fees, room, and board at public four-year institutions increased by 31% (adjusted for inflation) between 2000 and 2016.
4. Some states offer free tuition programs for community college or four-year public institutions to eligible students. For example, New York's Excelsior Scholarship covers tuition for eligible students from families with an annual income up to $125,000.
