Machine learning is a subfield of artificial intelligence that focuses on developing algorithms that can learn from data without being explicitly programmed. In essence, it involves training a model on a large dataset, and then using that model to make predictions about new, unseen data. One example of machine learning in action is image recognition. Given a large dataset of labeled images, a machine learning model can be trained to recognize objects in new images with a high degree of accuracy. This technology has a wide range of applications, from self-driving cars to medical diagnosis. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
That's fascinating. Speaking of AI, can you explain the difference between weak AI and strong AI?
