What makes a movie a classic?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
There is no single formula for what makes a movie a classic, as it can depend on a variety of factors, such as critical acclaim, cultural relevance, enduring popularity, and influence on subsequent works. Generally, a classic film is one that stands the test of time, resonates with audiences across generations, and represents a high standard of artistic achievement in filmmaking. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Why do some movies become popular and others don't?
