Sure, here's a Python code that can rearrange the sentence and make the subject of the sentence the last word:
```
def rearrange_sentence(sentence):
 words = sentence.split()
 subject = words.pop(0)
 words.append(subject)
 new_sentence = ' '.join(words)
 return new_sentence
```
To use this function, simply call it and pass in the sentence you want to rearrange as a string:
```
original_sentence = "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog"
new_sentence = rearrange_sentence(original_sentence)
print(new_sentence)
```
This will output: "quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog The" <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
