$int f(x) dx = F(x) + C$
In this formula, $f(x)$ is the function we want to integrate, $int$ represents the integral operator, $F(x)$ is the antiderivative of $f(x)$, and $C$ is the constant of integration. Can you use this formula to find the indefinite integral of the function $f(x) = 3x^2 + 4x - 2$?
