Can you explain the difference between supervised and unsupervised learning in machine learning?
Supervised learning is a technique used in machine learning where the algorithm learns from labeled data. In this technique, a model is trained using input-output pairs, and the algorithm adjusts its parameters to minimize the error between predicted output and actual output. On the other hand, unsupervised learning is a technique used in machine learning where the algorithm learns from unlabeled data. In this technique, the algorithm identifies patterns in the data without any prior knowledge of what it is looking for. Unsupervised learning algorithms are used for clustering, anomaly detection, and dimensionality reduction.
<|end|>
