<|user|>
Can you provide a recipe for a gluten-free chocolate cake using an excel table format? Please include ingredients, measurements, and cooking instructions.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here's a recipe for a gluten-free chocolate cake using an excel table format:
| Ingredients | Measurements |
| --- | --- |
| Gluten-free flour blend | 2 cups |
| Granulated sugar | 1 3/4 cups |
| Unsweetened cocoa powder | 3/4 cup |
| Baking powder | 1 1/2 tsp |
| Baking soda | 1 1/2 tsp |
| Salt | 1 tsp |
| Eggs | 2 |
| Milk | 1 cup |
| Vegetable oil | 1/2 cup |
| Vanilla extract | 2 tsp |
| Boiling water | 1 cup |
Instructions:
1. Preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C).
2. Grease two 9-inch round cake pans with cooking spray and line the bottoms with parchment paper.
3. In a large mixing bowl, whisk together the gluten-free flour blend, sugar, cocoa powder, baking powder, baking soda, and salt until well combined.
4. Add in the eggs, milk, vegetable oil, and vanilla extract. Mix until the batter is smooth and well combined.
5. Gradually pour in the boiling water, mixing until the batter is smooth and well combined.
6. Divide the batter evenly between the two prepared cake pans.
7. Bake for 30-35 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted into the center of the cakes comes out clean.
8. Remove the cakes from the oven and allow them to cool in the pans for 10 minutes.
9. Remove the cakes from the pans and transfer them to a wire rack to cool completely.
10. Once the cakes are cool, you can frost them with your favorite frosting and serve. Enjoy! <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How can I make a vegan version of this chocolate cake?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To make a vegan version of the gluten-free chocolate cake, you can replace the eggs with an egg substitute such as applesauce or mashed bananas. You can also use a non-dairy milk like almond or soy milk instead of regular milk, and vegetable oil in place of butter. Here's a modified recipe using these substitutions:

| Ingredients | Measurements |
| --- | --- |
| Gluten-free flour blend | 2 cups |
| Granulated sugar | 1 3/4 cups |
| Unsweetened cocoa powder | 3/4 cup |
| Baking powder | 1 1/2 tsp |
| Baking soda | 1 1/2 tsp |
| Salt | 1 tsp |
| Applesauce (or mashed banana) | 2/3 cup |
| Non-dairy milk (e.g. almond or soy milk) | 1 cup |
| Vegetable oil | 1/2 cup |
| Vanilla extract | 2 tsp |
| Boiling water | 1 cup |

Instructions:
1. Preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C).
2. Grease two 9-inch round cake pans with cooking spray and line the bottoms with parchment paper.
3. In a large mixing bowl, whisk together the gluten-free flour blend, sugar, cocoa powder, baking powder, baking soda, and salt until well combined.
4. Add in the applesauce (or mashed banana), non-dairy milk, vegetable oil, and vanilla extract. Mix until the batter is smooth and well combined.
5. Gradually pour in the boiling water, mixing until the batter is smooth and well combined.
6. Divide the batter evenly between the two prepared cake pans.
7. Bake for 30-35 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted into the center of the cakes comes out clean.
8. Remove the cakes from the oven and allow them to cool in the pans for 10 minutes.
9. Remove the cakes from the pans and transfer them to a wire rack to cool completely.
10. Once the cakes are cool, you can frost them with your favorite vegan frosting and serve.

Let me know if you have any other questions! <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




