Healthier Alternatives to Chocolate
Healthier Alternatives to Chocolate
===================================
Here are some tasty treats that are healthier than chocolate:
* Carob
-----
![Carob](https://i.imgur.com/3LgJmKz.jpg)
Carob is a sweet, nutty-tasting alternative to chocolate. It has a similar texture to chocolate and can be used in many of the same ways.
Nutritional information per 100g:
	+ Calories: 222
	+ Protein: 4.6g
	+ Fat: 0.6g
	+ Carbohydrates: 88g
	+ Fiber: 39gPotential health benefits:
	+ High in fiber
	+ Low in fat
	+ May help regulate blood sugar levelsPossible drawbacks:
	+ May cause digestive discomfort in some people
* Cacao Nibs
----------
![<|fim_suf|>](https://i.imgur.com/7CtTzZP.jpg)
Cacao nibs are small pieces of crushed cacao beans. They have a bitter, chocolatey taste and a crunchy texture.
Nutritional information per 100g:
	+ Calories: 272
	+ Protein: 4.9g
	+ Fat: 52g
	+ Carbohydrates: 34g
	+ Fiber: 33gPotential health benefits:
	+ High in fiber
	+ Rich in antioxidants
	+ May improve heart healthPossible drawbacks:
	+ High in fat and calories
	+ May be too bitter for some people
* Dark Chocolate
--------------
![Dark Chocolate](https://i.imgur.com/7v3qZgP.jpg)
Dark chocolate is a healthier alternative to milk chocolate. It has a rich, slightly bitter taste and a smooth texture.
Nutritional information per 100g:
	+ Calories: 598
	+ Protein: 7.8g
	+ Fat: 43g
	+ Carbohydrates: 46g
	+ Fiber: 11gPotential health benefits:
	+ Rich in antioxidants
	+ May improve heart health
	+ May improve brain functionPossible drawbacks:
	+ High in fat and calories
	+ May contain added sugar


```
I hope this helps! Let me know if you need anything else. <|endoftext|>
