<|asst|>
Of course! Here are some nut-free alternatives to chocolate:

1. Sunflower seed butter - This is a spread made from ground sunflower seeds. It has a creamy texture and a nutty flavor that is similar to peanut butter.

2. Tahini - Tahini is a paste made from ground sesame seeds. It has a rich, nutty flavor and can be used in a variety of recipes.

3. Coconut butter - Coconut butter is made from ground coconut meat. It has a smooth, creamy texture and a subtle coconut flavor.

4. Carob - As mentioned earlier, carob is a great alternative to chocolate for those with a nut allergy as it does not contain any nuts.

I hope this helps! <|endoftext|>
