<|fim_suf|>, promises, and async/await functions. Callback functions allow code to continue executing while waiting for an asynchronous task to complete. Promises represent a value that may not be available yet, allowing code to wait until the value is available before continuing. Async/await functions provide a way to write asynchronous code that looks similar to synchronous code, making it easier to reason about.

Overall, the choice between synchronous and asynchronous programming in JavaScript depends on the specific requirements of the task at hand. <|endoftext|>
