<|fim_suf|>, while flexible layouts allow your content to adapt to different screen sizes without breaking. Fluid images are images that scale with the size of their container, so they always fit within the available space.

One way to create a responsive layout is by using a flexible grid system like Bootstrap or Foundation. These frameworks provide a set of CSS classes that you can use to create columns and rows that adjust automatically based on the screen size. Another option is to use CSS Grid or Flexbox, which are built-in layout systems in CSS that allow you to create complex grid structures with less markup.

To make images responsive, you can use the `max-width` property to set the maximum width of the image to 100%, so it scales down as the screen gets smaller. You can also use the `srcset` attribute to provide multiple versions of an image at different resolutions, so the browser can choose the best one to display based on the screen size and resolution. <|endoftext|>
