Can you utilize C++ to solve this intricate puzzle? You are required to divide the list of words into sets of three based on their distinct characteristics. However, there's a twist - each set must contain words that share a common characteristic that is different from the previous set. Your task is to scrutinize the list of words provided below and start with the first set - Challenge, Champion, Chronic. Can you figure out what specific characteristic they share? To add complexity, ensure that the characteristic should not be used in the succeeding set. Keep going until all words are in sets of three. In addition to this, please provide the C++ code to execute this task. May success be on your side! 
The list of words: Challenge, Champion, Chronic, Developer, Denim, Disaster, Example, Elephant, Elite, Gadget.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, I can help you with that. The specific characteristic that Challenge, Champion, and Chronic share is that they all start with the letter "C". Here's the C++ code that can solve this puzzle:
```
#include 
#include 
#include 
#include 
using namespace std;
int main() {
 vector words = {"Challenge", "Champion", "Chronic", "Developer", "Denim", "Disaster", "Example", "Elephant", "Elite", "Gadget"};
 vector> sets;
 vector current_set;
 char current_char = 'A';
 for (int i = 0; i < words.size(); i++) {
 if (words[i][0] != current_char) {
 sets.push_back(current_set);
 current_set.clear();
 current_char = words[i][0];
 }
 current_set.push_back(words[i]);
 }
 sets.push_back(current_set);
 for (int i = 0; i < sets.size(); i++) {
 cout << "Set " << i + 1 << ": ";
 for (int j = 0; j < sets[i].size(); j++) {
 cout << sets[i][j] << " ";
 }
 cout << endl;
 }
 return 0;
}
```
