<|fim_suf|>, which can be detected by telescopes. Another method is through observing the motion of stars and gas in a galaxy. If their movements suggest the presence of a massive object with no visible source of light, it may indicate the presence of a black hole. Gravitational waves, ripples in space-time caused by the acceleration of massive objects, can also provide evidence for black hole mergers. <|endoftext|>
