<|asst|>
One of the main challenges that grocery stores face when increasing their stock of organic produce is sourcing enough supply to meet demand. Organic produce is typically more expensive and less abundant than conventionally grown produce, which can make it difficult for stores to offer consistent availability at reasonable prices. Additionally, perishability is a concern with fresh produce, so stores must manage their inventory carefully to avoid spoilage. <|endoftext|>
