```
#include 
#include 
using namespace std;
string convertToFormal(string sentence) {
 string modifiedSentence = sentence;
 size_t pos = modifiedSentence.find("requested to accomplish");
 if (pos != string::npos) {
 modifiedSentence.replace(pos, 22, "assigned to complete the task at hand");
 }
 return modifiedSentence;
}
int main() {
 string sentence = "I was requested to accomplish the task";
 string modifiedSentence = convertToFormal(sentence);
 cout << "Original sentence: " << sentence << endl;
 cout << "Modified sentence: " << modifiedSentence << endl;
 return 0;
}
```
In this code, the `convertToFormal` function accepts the original sentence as a string argument and returns the modified sentence as a string. The function uses the `find` and `replace` functions to locate the phrase "requested to accomplish" in the original sentence and replace it with "assigned to complete the task at hand". The modified sentence is then returned by the function.
In the `main` function, we call the `convertToFormal` function with the original sentence and print both the original and modified sentences to the console. 
