There is no single definition of intelligence among scientists, but some commonly cited definitions include the ability to learn from experience, adapt to new situations, reason and solve problems, comprehend complex ideas, and engage in abstract thinking. Some researchers also factor in traits like creativity, curiosity, and emotional intelligence when defining intelligence. <|endoftext|>
