 disp('The logical equation is true');
else
 disp('The logical equation is false');
end
```
In this code, we first define the values of A, B, and C. Then, we use an if statement to check if the logical equation (A AND B) OR (NOT C AND B) is true or false. If it's true, we display a message saying so. Otherwise, <|fim_suf|>, B, and C to test different scenarios and see how the logical equation evaluates. <|endoftext|>
