<|user|>
Can you modify the SQL query to retrieve declarative and interrogative sentences from the "sentences" table, where the "structure" column contains both the subject and object of the sentence, and the "text" column contains the predicate? Additionally, can you order the retrieved sentences based on the length of the predicate in ascending order?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Certainly! Here is the modified SQL query:
```
SELECT text
FROM sentences
WHERE structure LIKE '%subject%object%' 
AND (text LIKE '%?%' OR text LIKE '%.%')
ORDER BY LENGTH(text) ASC;
```
This query will retrieve all sentences from the "sentences" table where the "structure" column contains both the subject and object of the sentence, and the "text" column contains the predicate. The query also filters the results to only include declarative and interrogative sentences, by checking if the text column contains either a period or a question mark. Finally, the results are ordered based on the length of the predicate in ascending order. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
