<|fim_suf|>, and a unique code called a hash that identifies the block. When a new block is added to the chain, it's linked to the previous block using its hash. This creates a chain of blocks, hence the name "blockchain."

The security of the blockchain comes from the fact that once a block is added to the chain, it can't be altered or deleted without changing all subsequent blocks. This makes it virtually impossible for someone to tamper with the data without being detected.

One practical application of blockchain is cryptocurrency. Transactions are recorded on the blockchain, which ensures their validity and prevents fraud. 

