```python
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
# create a sample dataset
data = {'year': [2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020],
 'major': ['Computer Science', 'Business Administration', 'Engineering', 'Nursing', 'Psychology'],
 'graduates': [100, 150, 200, 250, 300]}
# convert the data to a pandas DataFrame
df = pd.DataFrame(data)
# create a bar chart
plt.bar(df['year'], df['graduates'])
# add title and labels
plt.title('Number of Graduates in the Last 5 Years')
plt.xlabel('Year')
plt.ylabel('Number of Graduates')
# show the chart
plt.show()
```
This code will create a bar chart with the year on the x-axis and the number of graduates on the y-axis. Each bar on the chart represents a year and the height of the bars corresponds to the total number of graduates for each year. The chart also includes a title and labels to make it more understandable. You can modify the code to use your own dataset. <|endoftext|>
