Can you explain why some people are allergic to bananas?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Banana allergy is relatively rare, but it can occur due to a variety of reasons. Some people have an allergy to the proteins found in bananas, which can trigger an immune system response. Others may have a sensitivity to the histamines found in bananas or may have an intolerance to the sugars found in ripe bananas. Additionally, some individuals with a latex allergy may experience cross-reactivity with bananas, as certain proteins in bananas are similar to those found in latex. <|endoftext|>
