```
val pairs = List((2, 8), (5, 1), (9, 3), (6, 7))
val smallestProducts = pairs.map(pair => pair._1 * pair._2)
val sum = smallestProducts.sum
println(sum)
```
To modify it, we can use the formula `pair._1.min(pair._2)` to find the smallest number in each pair, and then multiply them together. Here's the modified code:
```
val pairs = List((2, 8), (5, 1), (9, 3), (6, 7))
val smallestProducts = pairs.map(pair => pair._1.min(pair._2)).product
println(smallestProducts)
```
<|end|>
