How was the age of the universe calculated?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The age of the universe has been estimated through a variety of methods, including observations of the cosmic microwave background radiation, the ages of the oldest known stars, and measurements of the rate of expansion of the universe. One commonly used method is based on the observed distribution of galaxies and clusters of galaxies in the universe, which can be used to calculate the rate at which the universe has been expanding since the Big Bang. By extrapolating backwards in time from this rate, scientists have estimated that the age of the universe is approximately 13.8 billion years old. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
