Can you explain the difference between a metaphor and a simile?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Metaphors and similes are both figures of speech used to make a comparison between two things that are not alike. A metaphor is a figure of speech in which a word or phrase is applied to an object or action to which it is not literally applicable, whereas a simile is a figure of speech that compares two things using "like" or "as". For example, "Her hair is a field of wheat" is a metaphor, while "Her hair is like a field of wheat" is a simile. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
