<|asst|>
Denotation refers to the literal or dictionary definition of a word while connotation refers to the feelings and associations that a word evokes. For example, the denotation of the word "home" might be a place where one lives, but the connotation of the word can vary depending on personal experiences and cultural context. Some people might associate home with warmth and safety, while others might associate it with confinement or discomfort. <|endoftext|>
