<|user|>
How can I use JavaScript code to construct a list of five synonyms for the word "happy"?
Here's a sample JavaScript code that uses the Datamuse API to find synonyms for a given word:
const word = "happy";
const endpoint = `https://api.datamuse.com/words?rel_syn=${word}&max=5`;
fetch(endpoint)
 .then(response => response.json())
 .then(data => {
 const synonyms = data.map(word => word.word);
 console.log(synonyms);
 })
 .catch(error => console.log(error));
This code uses the fetch function to make a GET request to the Datamuse API, <|fim_mid|>passing in the word "happy" as a parameter for finding synonyms. It then retrieves the JSON response and extracts the first five synonyms from the array of objects returned. Finally<|fim_eom|>

