<|user|>
Can you explain the difference between precision and accuracy in scientific measurements?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Precision refers to the consistency or reproducibility of a measurement, while accuracy refers to how close a measurement is to the true value. A measurement can be precise but not accurate if it consistently gives the same result that is far from the true value. Similarly, a measurement can be accurate but not precise if it gives a result that is close to the true value but varies greatly each time it is measured. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
