Write a memoir excerpt from a former child actor who left Hollywood to pursue a career in science. Emma Watson
<|end|>
<|asst|>
I was only nine years old when I landed my first major role in a Hollywood film. It was a dream come true for me, something that I had always wanted since I was a little girl. I was thrilled to be a part of the entertainment industry, to work alongside some of the most talented actors and actresses in the world.
But as I grew older, I began to realize that there was more to life than just acting. I had always been fascinated by science and the natural world, and I knew that I wanted to pursue a career in that field. So, at the age of 18, I made the difficult decision to leave Hollywood and enroll in university to study science.
It wasn't an easy transition, of course. I had to adjust to a completely different lifestyle, one that was much more focused on academics and research than on glamour and fame. But I quickly fell in love with my studies, and I knew that I had made the right decision.
Looking back, I'm grateful for the experiences that I had as a child actor. I learned so much about the industry and about myself during that time. But I'm even more grateful for the opportunity to pursue my true passion in life. Science has given me a sense of purpose and fulfillment that I never could have found in Hollywood. And for that, I will always be grateful. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What was Emma Watson's experience like studying science at university after leaving Hollywood?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Emma Watson has spoken openly about her experience studying science at university after leaving Hollywood. She has said that it was a challenging but rewarding transition, and that she had to work very hard to catch up with her peers who had been studying science for years.
Watson also said that she felt a bit of imposter syndrome at first, as she was used to being in the spotlight as an actress and felt out of place in a room full of budding scientists. However, she credits her passion for learning and curiosity with helping her push through those initial feelings of uncertainty.
Despite the challenges, <|fim_suf|>, using her platform to raise awareness and inspire action. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


<|fim_mid|>Watson graduated from Brown University with a bachelor's degree in English literature and has continued to advocate for women in STEM fields. She has also been involved in various environmental and humanitarian causes<|fim_eom|>

